===========================================================================
  5. DATA PROTECTION & PRIVACY
===========================================================================

The Software handles personal data of SACCO members and borrowers
(including names, telephone numbers, national identification numbers,
addresses, photographs, and financial transactions). You are solely
responsible for:

  (a) obtaining lawful consent from data subjects before capture;
  (b) securing the data against unauthorised access, disclosure, or loss;
  (c) honouring data subject rights (access, correction, erasure);
  (d) reporting data breaches to the Personal Data Protection Office
      (PDPO) of Uganda within 72 hours of becoming aware of a breach; and
  (e) ensuring the hosting provider (e.g., GitHub Pages) complies with
      applicable data transfer rules.

The Licensor and Developer accept no responsibility for the manner in
which personal data captured through the Software is processed, stored,
or transferred.

===========================================================================
  6. REGULATORY COMPLIANCE
===========================================================================

The Software produces regulatory returns aligned to a common prudential
return structure for SACCOs in Uganda. However:

  (a) the benchmarks, provision rates, and templates shipped are
      indicative defaults only and may not match the latest UMRA
      guidelines or prescribed forms;

  (b) you are responsible for confirming all figures against the
      regulator's current requirements before submission; and

  (c) the Licensor and Developer make no representation that the
      Software's outputs will be accepted by any regulator, auditor, or
      financial examiner.

